1. Scope and definitions

"Licensor" means a copyright holder offering material under these terms.
"You" means a person or organisation exercising the permissions below.
"Covered Material" means the Zend Garden code, original artwork, models,
music, documentation and other material that the Licensor explicitly
provides under this licence, and adaptations of that material.
"Derivative Game" means a game or application that incorporates or adapts
Covered Material, including a modified version, port, expansion or fork.
An independent work merely distributed alongside Covered Material, without
incorporating or adapting it, is not a Derivative Game.

Material identified as belonging to a third party remains subject to its
own licence. These terms do not replace the licences of Godot, libraries,
tools, fonts or other independently licensed components. The Licensor
grants only rights that the Licensor has authority to grant. These terms
do not restrict rights you have under applicable law, including fair use
or fair dealing, or under a separate licence already granted to you.

2. Permission

Subject to these conditions, the Licensor grants you a worldwide,
non-exclusive, royalty-free copyright licence to use, run, study, copy,
modify, host and distribute Covered Material and to make and distribute
Derivative Games for noncommercial purposes. This grant lasts for the
duration of the applicable copyright unless terminated under section 7.
Noncommercial means not primarily intended for commercial advantage or
monetary compensation, subject to the express exceptions in section 5.

3. Free access and play

Covered Material and Derivative Games must be available to their users
without a required payment. You must not sell copies, charge for downloads
or source access, charge for playing or hosting access, or require a paid
subscription, membership, purchase, donation or bundle to access them.
You must not charge for gameplay features, levels, cosmetic items, virtual
currency, expansions or modifications containing Covered Material or
forming part of a Derivative Game. These restrictions apply regardless
of whether you operate for profit or as a nonprofit organisation.

You must not monetise Covered Material or a Derivative Game through
advertising, paid product placement or the sale of player data. Merely
using a hosting or distribution service that charges you, rather than
the game's users, does not breach this section.

4. Source availability and share-alike

Whenever you distribute or publicly host Covered Material or a Derivative
Game, you must make the complete corresponding source for the version
provided publicly downloadable without payment or compulsory registration.
Provide a clear source link with the distribution or in an accessible
place in the game or its hosting page. Keep that source available while
providing the version and for at least three years after you stop.

Corresponding source means the preferred editable form of all covered
code and assets, your modifications and additions forming the Derivative
Game, and scripts, project files and instructions reasonably necessary
to build and modify it. It includes editable model and artwork sources
where those are the preferred form for making changes. It does not
require publishing users' saved gardens, personal data, credentials or
unmodified general-purpose tools and independently licensed dependencies.
Identify dependencies and preserve their applicable licence notices.

You must provide your adaptations of Covered Material, and your code and
assets forming a Derivative Game, under this same licence. Recipients
must receive these same permissions and conditions, including free play,
source availability and share-alike for their own derivatives. Independent
third-party components may retain their own licences if those licences
permit distribution alongside these terms. You must not impose additional
terms or technological restrictions that prevent recipients from
exercising these permissions over Covered Material or the Derivative Game.
Private modifications that you neither distribute nor publicly host do
not require publication.

5. Donations, services and gameplay media

You may accept genuinely voluntary donations if all users have the same
access to the game, features, modifications and source whether or not
they donate. Donations must not purchase access, content or privileges.
You may charge for separately agreed support, teaching or development
services, provided payment is not required to access or play Covered
Material or a Derivative Game. Any Derivative Game distributed or publicly
hosted as a result of those services must satisfy these same conditions.

You may publish screenshots, gameplay videos, streams, reviews and
tutorials, including on monetised channels. This exception does not
permit selling playable games, code or asset files, or charging users
for access to a game or its features.

6. Notices and contributions

Keep the copyright notice, this licence and applicable third-party
notices with redistributed copies and source. Clearly describe your
changes and do not misrepresent a derivative as an official release.
No trademark permission or endorsement is granted.

Unless explicitly agreed otherwise, a contribution you intentionally
submit for inclusion in Covered Material is offered under this licence.
Contributors retain their copyright. This clause is not a copyright
assignment and does not grant permission to relicense their contributions
under different terms.

7. Termination and reinstatement

Your permissions terminate automatically if you breach these conditions.
For a first breach, they are reinstated if you stop the breach and remedy
it within 30 days of receiving notice. The Licensor may also expressly
reinstate them. Termination of your permissions does not terminate the
permissions of recipients who remain in compliance. If the Licensor
stops distributing the material, permissions already granted under this
licence continue for compliant recipients.

